Email Subject: Re: Regex issue with scoping in loops. 

Email Body: demerphq  wrote:
:Nobull (Brian McCauly) reports
[...]
:
:Here's a much simpler way to reproduce it
:
:use strict;
:use warnings;
:
:'From outside loop' ~ /(.*)/;
:
:for my $pass ( 1, 2 ) {
:    print "$1n";
:    'From later inside loop' ~ /(.*)/;
:}
:
:__END__
:
:The above could reasonably be expected to print 'From outside loop'
:twice but actually prints 'From later inside loop' the second time.
:
:The work-round is simply to double the {}
:
:use strict;
:use warnings;
:
:'From outside loop' ~ /(.*)/;
:
:for my $pass ( 1, 2 ) {{
:    print "$1n";
:    'From later inside loop' ~ /(.*)/;
:}}
:

